# Post-Edit Verification

## Tier 1 — Every AI-assisted change

Run `npm run lint`, `npm run test:run`, `npm run build`.
Verify all imports resolve to actual files (no hallucinated imports).
Run AI code bloat scan against the diff (see `bloat-scan.mdc`).
Confirm `git diff --name-only` matches stated task scope.
Confirm protected files (`LICENSE`, `CNAME`, `env.example`, `.env*`) are untouched.

## Tier 2 — UI / accessibility changes (add to Tier 1)

Tab through all new/changed interactive elements (keyboard-only walkthrough).
Verify accessible names and live region announcements with a screen reader.
Check all themes + `forced-colors: active` (high contrast mode).
Enable `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` and verify animations are suppressed.
Verify touch targets >= 44x44px.
Compare with existing components for visual consistency.

## Tier 3 — New features / major changes (add to Tier 1 + 2)

Verify OSS-first search was completed and documented (see `oss-first-search.mdc`).
Verify reference project linked in REFERENCES.md or via `@see`.
Verify non-trivial features have a feature flag.
Verify rollback procedure exists.
Draft CHANGELOG entry for user-facing changes.
Verify WCAG criteria addressed if UI changed.
Confirm no comprehension-critical tasks were delegated to subagents.
